From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 08:44:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7915: read the MT7915's implicit BF count from
 SDR33

Commit 15f9f88b ("mt76: mt7915: refine register definition") moved
MT_MIB_SDR33 from 0x08c to 0x088, which on the MT7915 is MIB SDR32, the
explicit beamforming count. Since then the MT7915's tx_pkt_ibf_cnt
statistic just repeated tx_pkt_ebf_cnt. The MT7916 and MT798x take
their implicit count from SDR32's upper half and don't use SDR33.

Put SDR33 back at 0x08c. Un-skip mt7915_test_mib_ibf_mt7915.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 mt7915/regs.h           | 2 +-
 mt7915/tests/mac-test.c | 7 ++-----
 2 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/mt7915/regs.h b/mt7915/regs.h
index dc7bb9a1..92c2e0d2 100644
--- a/mt7915/regs.h
+++ b/mt7915/regs.h
@@ -413,7 +413,7 @@ enum offs_rev {
 #define MT_MIB_SDR32_TX_PKT_EBF_CNT	GENMASK(15, 0)
 #define MT_MIB_SDR32_TX_PKT_IBF_CNT	GENMASK(31, 16)
 
-#define MT_MIB_SDR33(_band)		MT_WF_MIB(_band, 0x088)
+#define MT_MIB_SDR33(_band)		MT_WF_MIB(_band, 0x08c)
 #define MT_MIB_SDR33_TX_PKT_IBF_CNT	GENMASK(15, 0)
 
 #define MT_MIB_SDRMUBF(_band)		MT_WF_MIB(_band, __OFFS(MIB_SDRMUBF))
diff --git a/mt7915/tests/mac-test.c b/mt7915/tests/mac-test.c
index 4d8cdbb3..87e4f1c1 100644
--- a/mt7915/tests/mac-test.c
+++ b/mt7915/tests/mac-test.c
@@ -3889,17 +3889,14 @@ static void mt7915_test_mib_stats_mt7915(struct kunit *test)
 }
 
 /* MIB SDRn sits at 0x008 + 4 * n on the MT7915: SDR32 (explicit
- * beamforming) at 0x088, SDR33 (implicit) at 0x08c. The implicit count
- * must come from SDR33.
+ * beamforming) at 0x088, SDR33 (implicit) at 0x08c: the implicit count
+ * comes from SDR33.
  */
 static void mt7915_test_mib_ibf_mt7915(struct kunit *test)
 {
 	struct mt7915_test_env *env;
 	struct mt7915_dev *dev;
 
-	kunit_skip(test, "driver bug: MT7915 MT_MIB_SDR33 is 0x088 (SDR32), "
-		   "should be 0x08c since 15f9f88b; IBF count reads EBF");
-
 	env = mt7915_test_env_chip(test, 0x7915);
 	dev = env->dev;
 	mt76_wr(dev, MT_WF_MIB(0, 0x088), 5);
